    "['local-user [username] password cipher [password]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'username rta password 7 @%@%EDF~DAdfFD934J3<DAF#*<!@%@%', 'parent_command': ['aaa new-model'], 'root': 'aaa new-model', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the translated Cisco equivalent command for the Huawei configuration:\\n\\n##\\nusername rta password 7 @%@%EDF~DAdfFD934J3<DAF#*<!@%@%\\n##\\n\\nNotes:\\n1. In Cisco, \"7\" indicates that the password is encrypted (similar to Huawei\\'s \"cipher\" option)\\n2. The actual encrypted password string would remain the same (though Cisco might use a different encryption algorithm)\\n3. Cisco doesn\\'t have the exact same concept of \"local-user\" as Huawei, but \"username\" serves the equivalent purpose for PPP authentication', 'trans_template': 'username rta password 7 @%@%EDF~DAdfFD934J3<DAF#*<!@%@%'}]]": 1,
